Erick is an undergraduate student majoring in Mathematics of Data and Computing, 
with research interests in mathematical and computational modeling of biological 
systems. In the Camacho lab, he helps design, develop, and implement the lab's 
ERG data analysis pipeline, focusing primarily on the computational and dry-lab 
side of the workflow, while also shadowing other lab members to build broader 
wet-lab experience. Outside of the lab, Erick enjoys hiking, listening to 
music, and reading about history.
